2186488019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488151 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d5318616-df05-5cb7-9c1a-585554d2944f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{9}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "654ece2b-abda-569c-8738-da98c426c46e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488217 #edb/ref 1074 "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3)=P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=2)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,2)+f(3,4) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(3,2)=\\frac{9}{20}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(3)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $f(3,2)=\\frac{9}{20}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3) & =P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{9}{20})}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488308 #edb/ref 1058 #ed